Subject: [PATCH 19/37] feat: add broker gateway factory and package exports
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

broker.factory.get_gateway(settings) is the single place that turns
settings.broker into a concrete gateway instance — callers should
depend on this, never on a concrete gateway class directly, so broker
selection stays a configuration concern rather than a code-path one.
Raises ConfigurationError for an unrecognized broker or missing
required config (e.g. a Deriv token).

broker/__init__.py re-exports BrokerGateway, get_gateway, and every
DTO/enum as the package's public surface, with a docstring warning
against importing a concrete gateway class or broker SDK from outside
the package.

6 tests covering each broker selection path and configuration-error
cases.
